  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * @brief Convolution of Q7 sequences.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcA points to the first input sequence.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * @param[in] srcALen length of the first input sequence.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcB points to the second input sequence.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * @param[in] srcBLen length of the second input sequence.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst points to the location where the output result is written.  Length srcALen+src
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * @return none.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  *
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * @details
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  *
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * \par
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * The function is implemented using a 32-bit internal accumulator.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * Both the inputs are represented in 1.7 format and multiplications yield a 2.14 result.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * The 2.14 intermediate results are accumulated in a 32-bit accumulator in 18.14 format.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * This approach provides 17 guard bits and there is no risk of overflow as long as <code>max(srcAL
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * The 18.14 result is then truncated to 18.7 format by discarding the low 7 bits and then saturate
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  *
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * \par
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  * Refer the function <code>arm_conv_opt_q7()</code> for a faster implementation of this function.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  *
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_q7.c ****  */
